00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.710
And I remember Ricky saying something in that lunch that was really important.
我记得瑞奇在那次午餐上说了一句非常重要的话。

335
00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:39.930
He said, you know, in England, you can be really, really bad at your job for a long time, and
他说，你知道，在英国，你工作可以非常非常烂很长一段时间，

336
00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:40.970
you never get fired.
而且永远不会被开除。

337
00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.410
He's like, in America, that's going to frustrate people.
他说，在美国，这会让人感到沮丧。

338
00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.830
So my one piece of advice is that Michael can be a buffoon.
所以我给的一个建议是，迈克尔可以是个丑角。

339
00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:48.670
He can be silly.
他可以很滑稽。

340
00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:49.690
He can be irritating.
他可以很烦人。

341
00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:55.410
But you should, I suggest, he said that you show glimpses of him actually being a good
但我建议，他说，你们应该展现出他实际上擅长做销售的一些

342
00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:56.110
salesperson.
迹象。

343
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.050
And we do that throughout the show.
我们在整部剧中都这么做了。

344
00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:04.390
You see in future episodes that he is actually good at sales.
你在以后的剧集里会看到他其实很擅长销售。

345
00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.930
And he said that's going to be an important, I think, piece of the puzzle.
他说这将会是拼图中的一个重要部分，我想是的。

346
00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:14.830
And Stephen Merchant said, my piece of advice would be to lean a little bit more into the
斯蒂芬·莫昌特则说，我的建议是更多地倾斜于

347
00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.170
Jim and Pam relationship.
吉姆和帕姆的关系。

348
00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.230
He said-
他说—

349
00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.610
He knew the heart of it.
他抓住了核心。

350
00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.990
He said, that's really going to be the heart of your show.
他说，那将真正成为你们节目的核心。

351
00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:26.190
Because the British version, they did six episodes for their first season, six episodes for their
因为英国版的第一季拍了六集，第二季拍了六集

352
00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:28.550
second season, and one big Christmas special.
以及一个大型圣诞特别篇。

353
00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:32.930
And they knew that for American television, we were looking to do-
他们知道对于美国电视圈来说，我们打算拍——

354
00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:33.490
Years.
好几年。

355
00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:33.950
Years.
好几年。

356
00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.530
And we ended up doing 200.
而我们最后拍了二百集。

357
00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:39.150
So he said, you need to keep the heart beating on the show.
所以他说，你们得让这档节目的核心保持跳动。

358
00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.770
And so that's the heart of the show.
所以这就是节目的核心。

359
00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:42.530
That's Jim and Pam.
也就是吉姆和帕姆。

360
00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:44.230
Okay, I have another fast fact.
好的，我还有一个冷知识。

361
00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:48.770
We filmed the pilot six months before the rest of season one.
我们在第一季其余部分开拍六个月前就拍了试播集。

362
00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:54.070
And we shot it on the second floor of a real office building in Culver City.
而且我们是在卡尔弗城一栋真正办公楼的二楼拍的。

363
00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.290
So it was an actual office building.
所以这是一栋真正的办公楼。

364
00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:59.190
And a lot of times on sets, they build the office.
很多时候在片场，布景都是搭出来的。

365
00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.730
So if they want to film and get a certain camera angle, they can move a wall.
所以如果他们想拍某个特定的镜头角度，他们可以移开一面墙。

366
00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:03.610
They can move a window.
他们可以移开一扇窗。

367
00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.150
They can move a door because they built it.
他们可以移开一扇门，因为那是搭出来的。

368
00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:08.710
They actually say wall flying out and they move a whole wall.
他们甚至会喊“墙壁飞走”，然后把整面墙移开。

369
00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:09.490
They move a whole wall.
他们把整面墙都移开。

370
00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:10.070
It's insane.
这太疯狂了。

371
00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:14.270
On our show, because it was in an actual office building, you just had to work with it.
在我们的节目里，因为它是在真正的办公楼里拍的，你只能将就着拍。

372
00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.470
And it sort of really lended itself to the documentary style that all the shots weren't
这其实非常契合纪录片的风格，所有的镜头都不会

373
00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:19.170
going to look pretty.
显得那么唯美。

374
00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:23.290
They weren't going to be lined up just right because they had to work around actual walls
镜头不会排得刚刚好，因为他们必须绕过真正的墙壁

375
00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:24.110
and windows.
和窗户。

376
00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:25.570
They couldn't just pop them out.
他们不能随手把它们拆掉。

377
00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:31.770
I remember speaking to Ken Kwapis, our director, about setting certain rules for the documentary
我记得和我们的导演肯·夸皮斯谈过关于为纪录片

378
00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:32.910
style of filming.
拍摄风格设定某些规则的事。

379
00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:39.570
And he said it was very important to him that for all of the actors and the crew that the
他说这对他非常重要，对于所有演员和剧组来说，

380
00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:43.950
set felt like a real working office and a real documentary was happening.
片场感觉就像一个真正工作的办公室，就像真的在拍纪录片一样。

381
00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:49.650
And so one of the rules that he came up with was that he cleared the entire set of all crew
所以他想出的其中一个规则就是，他清空了整个片场的

382
00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:54.290
members except for a camera operator, a boom operator, and himself.
所有工作人员，只留下一个摄像师、一个录音师和他自己。

383
00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:54.890
Yes.
没错。

384
00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:55.690
And that was it.
就是这样。

385
00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:56.170
That was it.
就是这样。

386
00:14:56.190 --> 00:15:00.370
He also made all of the actors come in every morning, go through hair and makeup, and
他还让所有演员每天早上来，做完发型和化妆，

387
00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:04.830
then sit at our desks starting at 7.30 a.m., and we had to pretend to work.
然后从早上七点半开始坐在我们的办公桌前，我们必须假装在工作。

388
00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:05.830
Yes.
没错。

389
00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.690
And he walked around with the documentary crew and filmed us for 30 minutes.
然后他带着纪录片剧组四处走动，拍了我们三十分钟。

390
00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.610
Yeah, just us quietly working.
对，就是我们安安静静地工作。

391
00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:17.570
And little shots that you see, for example, of Pam doing whiteout, that is a piece of B-roll
你看到的那些零星镜头，比如帕姆用修正液的镜头，那就是

392
00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.830
from one of those working mornings that we did.
我们在那些工作早晨拍摄的垫片素材。

393
00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.510
And we did that every day on the pilot.
我们在拍试播集时每天都这么做。

394
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:27.670
Something else about this episode that I noticed is that there is a random exterior
关于这一集我还注意到另一件事，那就是有一个随机的

395
00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.410
shot of a building.
大楼外景镜头。

396
00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.090
Oh, Jenna, let me tell you.
哦，珍娜，我来告诉你吧。

397
00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:31.730
Well, wait, wait.
等等，等等。

398
00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.330
Let me grab one of my colorful note cards, as you call them.
让我拿一张你所说的我那五颜六色的便签卡。

399
00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:38.590
Exterior shot at 9.29, 9 minutes and 29 seconds.
9分29秒时的外景镜头，9分29秒。

400
00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:39.750
Not our building!
那不是我们的楼！

401
00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.410
With a huge exclamation point.
带着一个巨大的叹号。

402
00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:41.610
See?
看吧？

403
00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:42.670
This is a big discovery.
这是一个重大的发现。

404
00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:44.310
This is a big discovery for me.
对我来说这是一个重大的发现。

405
00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:49.330
Not only not our building, it wasn't the building we were filming in.
不仅不是我们的建筑，甚至不是我们拍摄时用的那栋楼。

406
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.790
I don't know where they got that shot.
我不知道他们是从哪弄来那个镜头的。

407
00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:51.050
I don't know.
我不知道。

408
00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.530
It's like stock footage from something?
这就像是某种素材库里的画面吧？

409
00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.710
I think it was stock footage.
我觉得那就是素材库画面。

410
00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.490
And then we never use it again.
然后我们就再也没用过它了。

411
00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:56.610
That was it.
就是这样。

412
00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:57.210
That was it.
就是这样。

413
00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.810
But they should go back and take that out.
但他们应该回去把它删掉。

414
00:15:58.930 --> 00:15:59.610
See you later.
回头见。

415
00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.890
And put a shot of the reels under Mifflin exterior.
然后在米夫林外观镜头下换上卷轴的画面。

416
00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.490
Jenna's getting sassy on you.
珍娜开始跟你顶嘴了呢。

417
00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:04.450
Yeah, I'm going to call someone.
对，我要给某人打电话。

418
00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.990
Someone get it right.
让别人来纠正一下。

419
00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:06.850
All right.
好吧。

420
00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:09.830
Here is my last fast fact for this episode.
这是我本集最后的冷知识。

421
00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:10.060
Okay, lady.
好吧，女士。

422
00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:10.150
Okay.
好的。

423
00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:12.710
Meredith is not Meredith.
梅雷迪思不是梅雷迪思。

424
00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:13.490
She is not.
她真不是。

425
00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.430
She is Henriette.
她是亨丽埃特。

426
00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:15.370
It's Henriette.
是亨丽埃特。

427
00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.010
Yes.
是的。

428
00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:21.910
Meredith is played by Henriette Mantell in the pilot episode, not Kate Flannery.
在试播集中，梅雷迪思由亨丽埃特·曼特尔饰演，而不是凯特·弗兰纳里。

429
00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.070
This is true.
千真万确。

430
00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:28.890
Henriette Mantell was a comedy actress who had just broken out because she had played Alice
亨丽埃特·曼特尔是一位喜剧女演员，她刚刚崭露头角，因为她曾在

431
00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.270
in the Brady Bunch filMs.
《脱线家族》电影中扮演爱丽丝。

432
00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.930
And she was there for the pilot.
她当时参与了试播集的拍摄。

433
00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:37.110
And then it was six months later that we got picked up.
然后过了六个月我们才获得续订。

434
00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:39.770
And then we started filming the rest of the episodes.
接着我们开始拍摄其余的剧集。

435
00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.470
And I guess the rumor was she was not available.
我猜传闻说她当时没空。

436
00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:43.010
She was busy.
她很忙。

437
00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:44.150
And we had to recast her.
我们不得不重新选角。

438
00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.730
And so Kate Flannery came in.
于是凯特·弗兰纳里加入了进来。

439
00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.030
Here is my fast fact.
这是我的冷知识。

440
00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.630
Kate Flannery and I met years before the office.
我和凯特·弗兰纳里在《办公室》开拍多年前就认识了。

441
00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.990
We were in a all-female improv group called Bitch Planet.
我们曾在一个名为“婊子星球”的全女性即兴喜剧团体里。

442
00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.110
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

443
00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.070
Aw, Bitch Planet.
噢，“婊子星球”。

444
00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:59.110
Sunday nights at like 10 p.m.
周日晚上大概10点。

445
00:16:59.170 --> 00:16:59.870
That's when you want to-
那就是你想——

446
00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.290
It's exactly when you want your comedy.
那正是你想看喜剧的时候。

447
00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.250
That's when you want to watch improv.
那正是你想看即兴表演的时候。

448
00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.350
Kate and I had known each other for a really long time.
我和凯特认识很久了。

449
00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:09.350
And also, Oscar Nunez and I did a sketch comedy show together called Hot Towel.
而且，奥斯卡·努涅斯和我曾一起做一个名为《热毛巾》的小品喜剧秀。

450
00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.130
Where do you get these names, Angela?
安吉拉，你都是从哪弄来这些名字的？

451
00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.430
So it was really fun for me because here I am.
所以对我来说这真的很有趣，因为我就在那里。

452
00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.490
Like, I was so nervous the first day.
天哪，我第一天紧张得要命。

453
00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:17.410
I didn't know Oscar had been caSt.
我当时不知道奥斯卡已经演员入选了。

454
00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.790
He didn't know I had been caSt.
他也不知道我已经入选了。

455
00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:20.510
You guys, this was sort of before-
各位，这有点像在——

456
00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.690
This was before smartphones.
这还是在智能手机出现之前。

457
00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:26.450
It's not like you texted someone you got a role or you put it on your social media.
不像现在，你得了角色会发短信告诉别人，或者发到社交媒体上。

458
00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.810
There was none of that.
当时根本没有这些。

459
00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:30.150
So you walked in and were completely surprised.
所以你走进去时完全被惊喜到了。

460
00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:32.190
I was completely surprised when I saw Oscar.
我看到奥斯卡的时候完全惊呆了。

461
00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:37.350
And not only did I see Oscar, but Ken Coapa sat us next to each other.
不仅看到了奥斯卡，肯·卡帕还把我们安排坐在一起。

462
00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.410
So I was like, oh my God, I'm going to be okay.
所以我当时想，哦天哪，我没问题了。

463
00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:40.430
That's amazing.
太棒了。

464
00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:41.390
My buddy's here.
我的哥们在这儿呢。

465
00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:44.110
And then Brian walked in as Kevin and I was like, here we go.
然后布莱恩作为凯文走了进来，我当时想，开始了。

466
00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:44.970
We're off to the races.
我们要全力以赴了。

467
00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.810
You guys were amazing in accounting.
你们在会计部演得太棒了。

468
00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:47.810
Thank you.
谢谢。

469
00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.610
I was sitting in my little corner back there.
我当时坐在后面的小角落里。

470
00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:00.590
I remember meeting everyone for the first time.
我记得第一次见到大家的情景。

471
00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:02.370
Do you remember your first impressions of people?
你们还记得对大家的第一印象吗？

472
00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:03.290
I do.
我记得。

473
00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.050
I remember my first impression of Rainn Wilson.
我记得我对雷恩·威尔逊的第一印象。

474
00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:05.870
Tell me.
快跟我说说。

475
00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.970
Well, I met Rainn Wilson at a live test audition.
嗯，我是在一次现场试镜中遇到雷恩·威尔逊的。

476
00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:15.210
So for all the leads of the show, they brought us into screen test and they mixed and matched us.
当时剧组把所有主要角色的候选人都叫去进行银幕试镜，把我们打乱重新组合。

477
00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.650
There were four Pams and four Dwights and four Jims and four Michaels.
当时有四个帕姆、四个德怀特、四个吉姆和四个迈克尔。

478
00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:19.010
Yeah.
对。

479
00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.890
And we spent an entire day being mixed and matched with each other.
我们花了一整天时间互相搭配试戏。

480
00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:30.230
And I remember I met Rainn Wilson and he was in character, but I couldn't really know that because I didn't know Rainn yet.
我记得我遇到了雷恩·威尔逊，他当时已经进入角色了，但我其实根本看不出来，因为我还不认识雷恩。

481
00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:35.090
And I thought he was the weirdest person I'd ever met in my life.
我觉得他是我这辈子见过最怪的人。

482
00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.710
Wait, he was in character the whole time?
等等，他全程都在角色里吗？

483
00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:37.090
Yeah.
对。

484
00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:38.370
He just was white.
他当时就是那种脸色苍白。

485
00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.130
Oh, so method, Rainn.
哦，雷恩可真够沉浸式表演的。

486
00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.650
He had his hair like that.
他当时留着那样的发型。

487
00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:41.910
So method.
太拼了。

488
00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:42.630
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

489
00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:44.330
I kind of did the same thing.
我其实也做了类似的事。

490
00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.090
I did my Pam hairstyle.
我弄了我的帕姆发型。

491
00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:52.030
The hairstyle that I wore on the show, I sort of invented through the audition process.
我在剧里梳的那款发型，其实是我在试镜过程中琢磨出来的。

492
00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:56.590
That sort of half up, half down, scrunchy, air-dried curl.
那种半扎半放、用发圈扎着、自然风干卷发的造型。

493
00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:58.970
And so I was very quiet.
所以我当时非常安静。

494
00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:06.010
I didn't talk to people in the waiting room because I just thought Pam was sort of not a chatter and I didn't want to get out of character.
我在候诊室里不跟别人说话，因为我觉得帕姆不是那种爱唠叨的人，而且我不想出戏。

495
00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.830
I remember one of the first things.
我记得其中的一件小事。

496
00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.950
This is so random, but it's true.
这听起来很随性，但确实是真的。

497
00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:15.170
That first week of filming, Rainn's wife came to have lunch.
拍摄的第一周，雷恩的妻子来探班吃午饭。

498
00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:21.170
And this is the main interaction I remember from Rainn during the pilot episode.
这是我对雷恩在拍试播集期间最深刻的互动记忆。

499
00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.870
Rainn introduced me to his wife.
雷恩把我介绍给了他妻子。

500
00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.170
She was pregnant at the time with their son.
她当时正怀着他们的儿子。

501
00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:26.610
Yes.
是的。

502
00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.270
And he said, this is my wife, Holly, bearer of my seed.
然后他说，这是我的妻子，霍莉，我骨肉的孕育者。

503
00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.080
And she started laughing.
然后她就笑了起来。

504
00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.360
But that was just Rainn being Rainn.
但这就是雷恩特有的风格。

505
00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:38.840
That's Rainn.
这就是雷恩。

506
00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:39.520
That is Rainn.
确实是雷恩。

507
00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:40.780
But wouldn't Dwight say that?
但迪怀特不也会这么说吗？

508
00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.060
He would also say that.
他也会这么说。

509
00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.260
This is Angela, bearer of my seed.
这是安吉拉，我骨肉的孕育者。

510
00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:43.780
Yes.
是的。

511
00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:44.400
It's amazing how...
真神奇，怎么……

512
00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.960
She's carrying my seed.
她怀着我的骨肉。

513
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.260
I'm like, oh my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

514
00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.980
I feel like we all had little parts of our characters in us.
我觉得我们每个人身上都有角色的一部分。

515
00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:54.700
But I don't know if that's true of you because you are so opposite from Angela Martin.
但我不知道这对你是否适用，因为你和安吉拉·马丁截然相反。

516
00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:55.220
I am.
我是的。

517
00:19:55.300 --> 00:20:01.340
I was thinking about how you were saying, like, you stayed in character and so did Rainn in between your auditions in the lobby.
我在想你刚才说的话，比如在试镜间隙，你和雷恩在休息室里都一直保持着角色状态。

518
00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.500
I would not have.
我可不会。

519
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:04.500
I would have been like, chitty chat chat.
我肯定会一直在那儿喋喋不休。

520
00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:05.380
Chitty chat chat.
喋喋不休。

521
00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:08.680
And then I would have just turned into a bitch when I entered the room.
然后一进房间，我就会立马变成个刻薄鬼。

522
00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:13.860
Well, you know, I didn't have any scenes with Rainn in the pilot of Substance.
好吧，你知道的，在《办公室》试播集中，我和雷恩没有任何对手戏。

523
00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.080
I didn't have any one-on-one scenes.
我没有任何一对一的戏份。

524
00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:22.040
So for me, when we were shooting the pilot, the people that I really bonded with were Steve, John, and you.
所以对我来说，当我们拍摄试播集时，真正建立起深厚感情的人是史蒂夫、约翰和你。

525
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.240
Because you were over the little part.
因为你就在那一小块区域。

526
00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.740
You were my closest seatmate in the office.
你是办公室里离我座位最近的人。

527
00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.140
So you and I bonded.
所以你和我建立了感情。

528
00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:34.600
And I remember after we finished the pilot and we all left and we didn't know if we were going to be picked up or make any more.
我记得在拍完试播集后，大家都散了，当时我们根本不知道这剧会不会被续订，也不知道还会不会有以后。

529
00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:37.420
Shortly after that, I turned 30 years old.
没过多久，我就迎来了30岁生日。

530
00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.580
It was a big milestone birthday for me.
对我来说这是一个非常重要的里程碑式的生日。

531
00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.460
And I really wondered if I should invite any of you guys.
我当时真的很纠结要不要邀请你们任何人。

532
00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.960
And I didn't.
而我没有。

533
00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:49.580
I didn't invite you guys because I thought, well, I'm probably never going to see them again.
我没有邀请你们，因为我想，好吧，我可能再也见不到他们了。

534
00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:53.300
Should I throw you another 30th birthday party and invite everyone?
要不我再为你办个30岁生日派对，把大家都请来？

535
00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.500
Would you?
你会吗？

536
00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:56.920
And then we could just say happy 30th.
然后我们就可以对你说句三十岁生日快乐。

537
00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:57.840
Will you?
你会吗？

538
00:20:58.420 --> 00:20:58.900
Okay.
好啊。

539
00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:04.580
Because now you guys are some of my closest friends and you aren't at my milestone birthday.
因为现在你们成了我最要好的朋友，而你们却没能参加我的重要生日。

540
00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.760
Okay, we'll have to throw you a 30th birthday party.
好吧，我们得给你补办一个30岁生日派对。

541
00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:08.660
It won't be weird.
一点也不会觉得奇怪。

542
00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:09.840
All right, guys.
好了，各位。

543
00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:13.320
So next up, we are going to break down this episode.
接下来，我们要剖析这一集。

544
00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:14.980
We're going to really get into the nitty-gritty.
我们要深入探讨其中的细节。

545
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.420
We're going to talk about scenes and memories and stories.
我们要聊聊那些场景、回忆和故事。

546
00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.240
So stick with us.
所以请继续关注我们。

547
00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:27.320
We're talking about the pilot episode of The Office.
我们要聊的是《办公室》的试播集。

548
00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:30.340
And I think we should talk about some of our favorite moments, Jenna.
我觉得我们应该聊聊一些我们最喜欢的时刻，珍娜。

549
00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:30.920
Yes.
好的。

550
00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.160
Well, one of my favorite moments is the dynamic between Pam and Michael.
嗯，我最喜欢的时刻之一就是帕姆和迈克尔之间的互动。

551
00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:37.420
I mean, selfishly, I guess I'm in that moment.
我的意思是，出于私心，我想我正处于那个时刻。

552
00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:40.360
But I really loved working with Steve Carell.
但我真的很喜欢和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔合作。

553
00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:45.140
I really loved how much he let me be silent and just look at him.
我真的很喜欢他那么信任我，让我保持沉默，只是看着他。

554
00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:45.980
And just react.
只是做出反应。

555
00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:46.460
Yes.
是的。

556
00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.340
I loved that.
我太喜欢了。

557
00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:53.380
But I especially love whenever Melora Hardin, who plays Jan Levinson Gould, got in the mix.
但我尤其喜欢梅洛拉·哈尔丁饰演的简·莱文森·古尔德加入进来的那些戏份。

558
00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:54.680
She's so commanding.
她太有气场了。

559
00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.900
Just like Melora's presence is like, I'm scared of her.
梅洛拉的存在感就好像是，我都有点怕她。

560
00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:58.340
Yes.
是的。

561
00:21:58.520 --> 00:21:59.000
I get it.
我懂。

562
00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.000
I get why he was a little scared of her.
我理解为什么他会有点怕她。

563
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:08.200
And I love the scene where Michael tries to throw Pam under the bus about why he doesn't have the agenda that he's supposed to have.
我很喜欢迈克尔试图把帕姆推出来当替罪羊的那场戏，因为他没有准备好本该准备的议程。

564
00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:14.580
And it's because he told her to throw it in the receptacle, the trash can that is a special filing cabinet for corporate memos.
原因是他告诉帕姆把它扔进容器里，也就是那个专门用来存放公司备忘录的垃圾桶。

565
00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.260
And I remember shooting that scene.
我记得当时拍摄那场戏的情景。

566
00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:26.480
And I just remember every time that Pam said, you told me to put it in a special filing cabinet that is a trash can, that we would giggle.
我只记得每次帕姆说“你让我把它放进那个作为垃圾桶的特殊文件柜里”时，我们都会咯咯笑个不停。

567
00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:33.440
And so I just remember the matter-of-factness of that moment and how fun that was.
所以我只记得那个时刻那种一本正经的感觉，以及当时是多么有趣。

568
00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:36.540
Pam totally stood up for herself in her own little way in that moment.
帕姆在那一刻用她自己的小方式彻底为自己挺身而出了。

569
00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:38.140
Here's the thing about Steve Carell.
关于史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，事情是这样的。

570
00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:40.900
He is one of the nicest people you will ever meet.
他是你所能遇到最好的人之一。

571
00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:42.280
He is so nice.
他人真的太好了。

572
00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:46.020
I know it's almost even become like a joke, like Steve Carell's the nicest person ever.
我知道这甚至快成了一个笑话，就像说史蒂夫·卡瑞尔是史上最好的人一样。

573
00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:47.140
But he is.
但他真的是。

574
00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:47.580
I know.
我懂。

575
00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.220
And people ask me a lot, what's it like to work with Steve Carell?
人们经常问我，和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔一起工作是什么感觉？

576
00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:51.940
Are you just laughing all the time?
你们是不是一直在笑？

577
00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:56.320
And no, you're not laughing all the time because Steve isn't on all the time.
并不是，你们并没有一直在笑，因为史蒂夫并不是无时无刻都在搞笑。

578
00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:57.340
He's not one of those—
他不是那种——

579
00:22:57.340 --> 00:22:57.760
He's a real person.
他是个真实的人。

580
00:22:57.760 --> 00:22:58.620
He's a real person.
他是个真实的人。

581
00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:02.280
And he's—I've worked with comedians who are on all the time.
而且他——我跟那些无时无刻不在搞笑的喜剧演员合作过。

582
00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:02.480
Yeah.
是的。

583
00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:06.500
Who walk around and you can just—they can't turn off their joke-making brain.
他们四处走动，你就能——他们的搞笑大脑根本停不下来。

584
00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:07.400
I drive my cursor.
我把光标移过去。

585
00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:08.660
It's a little insane.
这有点疯狂。

586
00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:10.240
Steve is not like that.
史蒂夫可不是那样。

587
00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:16.880
But you and Steve and I would sit and have long conversations about the best frozen yogurt in the San Fernando Valley.
但你、我和史蒂夫会坐在一起，长时间地聊圣费尔南多谷最好吃的冻酸奶。

588
00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:24.340
Oh, I will never forget the morning—on Monday mornings, Steve would come out of his office, out of Michael Scott's office between scenes.
哦，我永远不会忘记那个早晨——在周一早晨，两场戏的间隙，史蒂夫会从他的办公室，从迈克尔·斯科特的办公室里走出来。

589
00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:27.640
He would walk over to Jenna and I, and we would talk about our weekends.
他会走向珍娜和我，然后我们就会聊起各自的周末。

590
00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:32.080
And one Monday morning, he walked over, and he was like, ladies, guess what I did this weekend?
就在某个周一早晨，他走过来，说道，女士们，猜猜我这个周末做了什么？

591
00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:32.560
We're like, what?
我们问，什么？

592
00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:33.800
And he goes, I went to Target.
他说，我去了塔吉特百货。

593
00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:35.860
And he would talk to us about Target.
然后他会跟我们聊起塔吉特的事。

594
00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:37.460
And he told us about his Target run.
他跟我们讲了他去塔吉特的经历。

595
00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:39.520
It was really, really sweet.
真的非常非常甜心。

596
00:23:39.760 --> 00:23:48.060
You know, recently, I was in a Michaels purchasing some supplies for a crafting job, and the checkout guy said,
你知道，最近我在一家迈克尔斯工艺品店买一些做手工的材料，收银员说，

597
00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:51.360
oh, my gosh, now this is getting crazy.
天哪，这下太疯狂了。

598
00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:54.160
This morning, Oscar Nunez came in here.
今天早上奥斯卡·努涅斯来过这里。

599
00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:56.400
Then Steve Carell, and now you?
然后是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，现在又是你？

600
00:23:56.580 --> 00:23:57.800
What, do you guys all live here?
怎么，你们这群人全住在这是吗？

601
00:23:57.960 --> 00:23:59.600
We love crafting.
我们热爱手工。

602
00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:01.080
We love crafting.
我们热爱手工。

603
00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:02.360
And we're all here.
我们都在这儿。

604
00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:06.580
We're all sort of—I guess we all live around this one Michaels crafting store.
我们基本上——我想我们都住在迈克尔手工艺品店附近。

605
00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:06.820
Yeah.
是啊。

606
00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:13.200
I texted Steve, and I said, Steve, the checkout guy at Michaels told me you were buying some crafting supplies today.
我发短信给史蒂夫，我说，史蒂夫，迈克尔的收银员告诉我你今天买了一些手工艺品。

607
00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:15.940
And he said, oh, yes, I needed some glue sticks.
他说，哦，对，我需要一些热熔胶棒。

608
00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:17.720
He sort of told me what he needed.
他大致跟我说了他需要什么。

609
00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.020
He's like, what were you there for?
他好像在问，你当时去那儿干嘛？

610
00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:21.140
But that is Steve.
不过这就是史蒂夫。

611
00:24:21.260 --> 00:24:21.980
That is Steve.
这就是史蒂夫。

612
00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:23.940
That's the kind of stuff we would talk to him about.
这就是我们会跟他聊的那种事。

613
00:24:23.940 --> 00:24:31.240
And so to then—to have that man then shift into this scene where he's just being awful to my character.
所以后来——当这个男人转变成这种对我的角色极其恶劣的场景时。

614
00:24:31.500 --> 00:24:34.580
Like throwing you under the bus in front of the big boss lady.
就像在大老板女上司面前把你给出卖了一样。

615
00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:38.060
Yes, when our real dynamic was just like so much—
是的，而我们真实的相处模式明明是那么——

616
00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:38.640
So, so different.
完全，完全不同。

617
00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:39.280
So much love.
充满了爱。

618
00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:43.600
So in the scene, Jan tells Michael there's going to be downsizing.
所以在这一场戏里，简告诉迈克尔将要进行裁员。

619
00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:43.800
Yeah.
是啊。

620
00:24:43.900 --> 00:24:44.980
This is big news.
这是个大新闻。

621
00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:45.520
Big news.
大新闻。

622
00:24:45.640 --> 00:24:46.100
This is important.
这很重要。

623
00:24:46.660 --> 00:24:48.200
Michael should be paying attention.
迈克尔本该认真听着的。

624
00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:51.300
We've already established that he's thrown away the agenda for the meeting.
我们之前已经确认过他把会议议程给扔了。

625
00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:52.720
Yeah, he should take this seriously.
对啊，他该重视起来的。

626
00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:56.220
But instead, he takes a phone call from his friend, Todd Packer.
但相反，他接起了他朋友托德·帕克尔的电话。

627
00:24:56.340 --> 00:25:00.220
Todd Packer, his party buddy, who he clearly covets.
托德·帕克尔，他的派对酒肉朋友，他显然对人家艳羡不已。

628
00:25:00.400 --> 00:25:01.580
He thinks this guy's amazing.
他觉得这家伙太棒了。

629
00:25:01.840 --> 00:25:08.500
Another interesting fact about this scene is that the voice of Todd Packer that comes on the phone
关于这场戏另一个有趣的事实是，电话里传出的托德·帕克尔的声音

630
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:13.380
is not the voice of the real Todd Packer.
并不是真正的托德·帕克尔的声音。

631
00:25:13.540 --> 00:25:15.160
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

632
00:25:15.340 --> 00:25:18.420
Dave Koechner ends up playing Todd Packer.
最后是戴夫·科克纳饰演的托德·帕克尔。

633
00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:23.020
When we meet him in season two, this role is played by Dave Koechner.
